<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>Latest news from the Middle East, daily international news reports - France 24</title><description>FRANCE 24’s coverage and analyses of political and social issues across the Middle East, including Egypt, the Gulf states, Iraq, Israel, Jordan, Lebanon, Saudi Arabia, Syria, Yemen and beyond.</description><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/</link><lastBuildDate>Mon, 12 Oct 2026 17:49:58 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category></category><title>Saudi Arabia extends Riyadh aiport suspension, vows deadly response to Houthis strikes</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/saudi-arabia-extends-riyadh-aiport-suspension-vows-deadly-response-to-houthis-strikes</link><description>
Saudi Arabia extended on Monday the closure of the international airport in Riyadh after announcing the Saudi-led coalition was responding to Houthi combined drone and missile attacks. On Saturday, another attack left 13 dead and over 300 injured. This is one of the worst disruptions to Saudi aviation in years – marking a significant escalation in the war with Yemen's Houthi rebels. Details and analysis by FRANCE 24 international affairs editor Philip Turle.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8e087024-c657-11f1-b925-77317c09f325/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261012-170113-170804-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8e087024-c657-11f1-b925-77317c09f325/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261012-170113-170804-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">930a6d16-c657-11f1-ad31-37097af3614a</guid><pubDate>Mon, 12 Oct 2026 16:21:57 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>The Observers</category><title>Concerts of pro-Assad singers cancelled in Syria</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-observers/20261012-concerts-pro-assad-singers-cancelled</link><description>
The concerts of several singers accused of supporting the regime of deposed president Bashar al-Assad have been cancelled this summer in Syria. People in Homs ripped down posters advertising performances by artists Mohamad Iskandar and Hossam Jneed, denouncing their previous links with the regime. One of the musicians later publicly apologised. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/71e2a3a2-c624-11f1-a2f5-3774aeac812a/w:1024/p:16x9/vlcsnap-2026-10-12-11h47m40s172.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/71e2a3a2-c624-11f1-a2f5-3774aeac812a/w:1024/p:16x9/vlcsnap-2026-10-12-11h47m40s172.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">c4228538-c624-11f1-a08d-f15a4abace13</guid><pubDate>Mon, 12 Oct 2026 13:53:58 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>The FRANCE 24 Observers</dc:creator></item><item><category>Perspective</category><title>'Perfect Victims' author Mohammed El-Kurd challenges how Palestinian suffering is viewed</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/perspective/20261012-perfect-victims-author-mohammed-el-kurd-challenges-how-palestinian-suffering-is-viewed</link><description>
Mohammed El-Kurd is a Palestinian writer, poet and journalist. He is the author of the poetry collection Rifqa and the book "Perfect Victims and the Politics of Appeal", which was just published in French translation last week. Mohammed grew up in Sheikh Jarrah in East Jerusalem and as a child, his family were displaced from their home by Israeli settlers in a high-profile eviction. He spoke to us in Perspective.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d41606a0-c63c-11f1-ac79-e362370cce2e/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-18157455296accd9cdf27ba1-37613308.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d41606a0-c63c-11f1-ac79-e362370cce2e/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-18157455296accd9cdf27ba1-37613308.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">70462e7c-c626-11f1-9854-7b78552cd9fc</guid><pubDate>Mon, 12 Oct 2026 13:12:47 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Oliver FARRY</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Netanyahu demands probe into Israeli anonymous whistleblowers in 'NAZA' documentary</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/netanyahu-demands-probe-into-israeli-anonymous-whistleblowers-in-naza-documentary</link><description>
Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu on Sunday called for an investigation into the anonymous sources featured in the award-winning Gaza war documentary "NAZA". The film, which won the Special Jury Prize at the Venice Film Festival last month, is based on testimony from 24 unnamed Israeli military whistleblowers who accuse the army of killing numerous civilians in Gaza with the use of AI-powered targeting systems. Details by FRANCE 24 correspondent in Jerusalem, Noga Tarnopolsky.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f9ad5328-c62d-11f1-ac7e-3774aeac812a/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261012-100856-101124-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f9ad5328-c62d-11f1-ac7e-3774aeac812a/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261012-100856-101124-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ff72ecb4-c62d-11f1-9d3e-4900808bc323</guid><pubDate>Mon, 12 Oct 2026 11:17:27 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Saudi Arabia: Riyadh airport struck again by Yemen's Houthis</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/saudi-arabia-riyadh-airport-struck-again-by-yemen-s-houthis</link><description>
A new attack hit Riyadh's international airport on Sunday, a day after another attack on the airport killed at least 12 people and injured over 300. This was the deadliest on Saudi soil in over a decade. Fighting between the Iran-backed Houthis and Saudi-backed Yemeni government forces have been escalating for several weeks. Story by Juliette Brown and Caitlin Brown.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/234f8a80-c61e-11f1-bf35-3774aeac812a/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-11T224410Z-1659588386-RC241OAGCJLV-RTRMADP-3-IRAN-CRISIS-SAUDI-AIRPORT.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/234f8a80-c61e-11f1-bf35-3774aeac812a/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-11T224410Z-1659588386-RC241OAGCJLV-RTRMADP-3-IRAN-CRISIS-SAUDI-AIRPORT.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b709347a-c61d-11f1-bb18-637269ba2545</guid><pubDate>Mon, 12 Oct 2026 09:21:12 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Live: Riyadh airport to remain closed after deadly Houthi attacks</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261012-live-saudi-arabia-extends-suspension-of-operations-at-riyadh-airport-after-deadly-houthi-attacks</link><description>
Saudi Arabia's civil aviation body extended the suspension of operations at Riyadh's international airport Monday following a series of deadly attacks by Yemen's Iran-aligned Houthi rebels over the weekend. The statement announcing the decision did not specify when operations would resume. Follow our liveblog for the latest developments.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c294b8ba-c5ae-11f1-9976-77317c09f325/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-11T133451Z-158209492-RC211OAHP5D3-RTRMADP-3-IRAN-CRISIS-SAUDI-AIRPORT.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c294b8ba-c5ae-11f1-9976-77317c09f325/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-11T133451Z-158209492-RC211OAHP5D3-RTRMADP-3-IRAN-CRISIS-SAUDI-AIRPORT.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">c7ce9790-c5d3-11f1-b586-fb36e88e0e35</guid><pubDate>Mon, 12 Oct 2026 08:41:12 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c294b8ba-c5ae-11f1-9976-77317c09f325/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-11T133451Z-158209492-RC211OAHP5D3-RTRMADP-3-IRAN-CRISIS-SAUDI-AIRPORT.jpg">© Social Media via Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Fresh Houthi strike hits Riyadh airport a day after deadly attack</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261012-houthi-strike-riyadh-airport-yemen</link><description>
A fresh Houthi strike hit Riyadh’s King Khalid International Airport on Sunday, killing a Pakistani resident and wounding 11, Saudi authorities said. The attack followed a strike that killed at least 12 people and halted airport operations on Saturday. The Iran-backed group threatened further attacks on Saudi Arabia’s transit hubs.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c294b8ba-c5ae-11f1-9976-77317c09f325/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-11T133451Z-158209492-RC211OAHP5D3-RTRMADP-3-IRAN-CRISIS-SAUDI-AIRPORT.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c294b8ba-c5ae-11f1-9976-77317c09f325/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-11T133451Z-158209492-RC211OAHP5D3-RTRMADP-3-IRAN-CRISIS-SAUDI-AIRPORT.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">adc8ce1e-c5cf-11f1-a257-89d8aea9124d</guid><pubDate>Mon, 12 Oct 2026 01:01:39 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c294b8ba-c5ae-11f1-9976-77317c09f325/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-11T133451Z-158209492-RC211OAHP5D3-RTRMADP-3-IRAN-CRISIS-SAUDI-AIRPORT.jpg">© Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Escalating fighting in Yemen worsens food security crisis</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/escalating-fighting-in-yemen-worsens-food-security-crisis</link><description>
Aid agencies in Yemen highlighted the growing hunger emergency sparked by renewed fighting between Houthi opposition forces and Government troops, after mobile health clinics reported that hundreds of children displaced by the violence are suffering from the most deadly form of malnutrition.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4ec9538a-c53d-11f1-afd5-e362370cce2e/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261011-080348-080521-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4ec9538a-c53d-11f1-afd5-e362370cce2e/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261011-080348-080521-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">534db6e4-c53d-11f1-ad6d-15d0d6d37d45</guid><pubDate>Sun, 11 Oct 2026 06:34:05 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Saudi Arabia threatens 'decisive' response after Riyadh airport strike kills at least 12</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261011-riyadh-airport-strike-kills-12-saudi-arabia-threatens-decisive-response</link><description>
Saudi Arabia vowed to retaliate against Yemen’s Houthi rebels on Sunday after a strike on Riyadh’s international airport killed a dozen people and wounded more than 300, marking the kingdom's deadliest strike in a decade.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f5c423ba-b42e-11f1-9171-6f779f079bc8/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-19T114800Z-1100229945-RC28MNAOL58F-RTRMADP-3-IRAN-CRISIS-SAUDI-YEMEN.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f5c423ba-b42e-11f1-9171-6f779f079bc8/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-19T114800Z-1100229945-RC28MNAOL58F-RTRMADP-3-IRAN-CRISIS-SAUDI-YEMEN.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">7e70621c-c539-11f1-b6fc-57b5bb5be337</guid><pubDate>Sun, 11 Oct 2026 06:21:50 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f5c423ba-b42e-11f1-9171-6f779f079bc8/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-19T114800Z-1100229945-RC28MNAOL58F-RTRMADP-3-IRAN-CRISIS-SAUDI-YEMEN.jpg">© Stringer, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Riyadh airport strike kills 12, Saudi Arabia threatens 'decisive' response</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261011-at-least-twelve-killed-multiple-people-wounded-in-attack-on-riyadh-airport-1</link><description>
Saudi Arabia vowed to retaliate against Yemen’s Houthi rebels on Sunday after a strike on Riyadh’s international airport killed a dozen people and wounded more than 300, marking the kingdom's deadliest strike in a decade.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6a8b286a-c532-11f1-b166-29a2e29ae696/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261011-060136-060302-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6a8b286a-c532-11f1-b166-29a2e29ae696/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261011-060136-060302-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">6ff26e8a-c532-11f1-9d4b-b30d91264429</guid><pubDate>Sun, 11 Oct 2026 05:16:22 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Houthi rebels claim latest attacks on Riyadh airport, following Saturday's deadly strike</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261011-live-saudi-arabia-vows-decisive-response-after-deadly-houthi-strike-on-riyadh-airport</link><description>
Yemen's Houthis have claimed responsibility for attacks on Riyadh's international airport on Sunday, which the Saudi Civil Aviation Authority reported as having caused injuries. The attacks follow Saturday’s strike on the civilian airport which killed at least 12, constituting the deadliest on Saudi soil in more than a decade. Read our blog to see how the day's events unfolded.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0521e248-c550-11f1-8562-29a2e29ae696/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-02-17T000000Z-191424583-MT1IMGOST000OXOJ1D-RTRMADP-3-IMAGO-IMAGES.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0521e248-c550-11f1-8562-29a2e29ae696/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-02-17T000000Z-191424583-MT1IMGOST000OXOJ1D-RTRMADP-3-IMAGO-IMAGES.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a64eb6c0-c530-11f1-814f-61908b950495</guid><pubDate>Sun, 11 Oct 2026 05:04:26 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0521e248-c550-11f1-8562-29a2e29ae696/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-02-17T000000Z-191424583-MT1IMGOST000OXOJ1D-RTRMADP-3-IMAGO-IMAGES.jpg">© Markus Mainka, Imago via Reuters</source><dc:creator>Anaëlle JONAH</dc:creator></item><item><category>Spotlight</category><title>Why Yemen's war is escalating</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261010-spotlight</link><description>
Loud explosions have been heard at Riyadh airport. Diplomatic sources say that Yemen's Houthi fighters have launched another missile attack on the international hub. At least five people have been treated for extensive injuries, according to hospital sources, with dozens more injured. The Saudi government hasn't yet commented, as more airlines cancel flights to the country. Meanwhile, Saudi jets continue to strike Yemen, in support of the Yemeni government involved in fierce fighting to push back Houthi positions.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/52ff5d46-c4d4-11f1-a7b0-e362370cce2e/w:1024/p:16x9/Houthi-000-D2RW9CQ.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/52ff5d46-c4d4-11f1-a7b0-e362370cce2e/w:1024/p:16x9/Houthi-000-D2RW9CQ.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0d9708a0-c4cd-11f1-9e5c-477a06fce4ea</guid><pubDate>Sat, 10 Oct 2026 18:22:23 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Gavin LEE</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>At least twelve killed, multiple people wounded in attack on Riyadh airport</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261010-riyadh-airport-suspends-operations-after-attack-leaves-multiple-people-wounded</link><description>
At least twelve people were killed in an attack on Riyadh's King Khalid International Airport on Saturday, including an Egyptian flight attendant, according to a medical source at a local hospital. Earlier this week, another attack on the airport by the Houthis killed three people and damaged a plane, though the Iran-backed group did not announce any new attacks on Saturday.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a3556cb4-c4d3-11f1-90a7-53993c5f1f18/w:1024/p:16x9/AP314998123886.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a3556cb4-c4d3-11f1-90a7-53993c5f1f18/w:1024/p:16x9/AP314998123886.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0a40824c-c4ca-11f1-a6da-91b86ff72895</guid><pubDate>Sat, 10 Oct 2026 18:03:32 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a3556cb4-c4d3-11f1-90a7-53993c5f1f18/w:1024/p:16x9/AP314998123886.jpg">© Carolyn Kaster, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Yemen says advancing against Houthis around key Bab al-Mandab strait</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261010-yemen-says-forces-made-advances-against-houthis-around-key-waterway</link><description>
Yemen said Saturday that forces were advancing against the Houthis around the Bab al-Mandab strait, a week after the country's Saudi-backed government announced that it was initiating a counter-offensive to take back territory seized by the pro-Iran group during last month's lightning offensive. In Riyadh, diplomatic sources reported a missile attack on the civilian airport, with at least five Saudi nationals wounded being treated in intensive care. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/63b80868-c4ac-11f1-b128-29a2e29ae696/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26279449082196.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/63b80868-c4ac-11f1-b128-29a2e29ae696/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26279449082196.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d761d14c-c4aa-11f1-acd0-877b784b702e</guid><pubDate>Sat, 10 Oct 2026 13:45:14 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/63b80868-c4ac-11f1-b128-29a2e29ae696/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26279449082196.jpg">© Southern Giants Brigades Media Office via AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Palestinian president Abbas postpones legislative, presidential elections to September 2027</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261010-palestinian-president-abbas-postpones-legislative-elections-to-september-2027</link><description>
⁠⁠Palestinian president ​Mahmoud ​Abbas announced on Saturday that legislative ⁠elections would be postponed from November ​28 to September ​11, 2027, the ​official Palestinian news agency ⁠WAFA reported. In his presidential decree, Abbas set the next presidential elections for that day as well.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/68f8bf20-b818-11f1-a7c2-4d88a6d99c48/w:1024/p:16x9/AP25356421415725.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/68f8bf20-b818-11f1-a7c2-4d88a6d99c48/w:1024/p:16x9/AP25356421415725.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">5813cf5c-c4a1-11f1-9901-7958fca43b77</guid><pubDate>Sat, 10 Oct 2026 11:56:40 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/68f8bf20-b818-11f1-a7c2-4d88a6d99c48/w:1024/p:16x9/AP25356421415725.jpg">© Nasser Nasser; AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Palestinians struggle to find food in Gaza a year after ceasefire</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261010-hunger-and-malnutrition-stalk-gazans-a-year-on-from-ceasefire</link><description>
Widespread hunger remains persistent in the Gaza Strip despite the ceasefire agreement between Hamas and Israel a year ago that was supposed to allow more food into the Palestinian territory. A new study published on Thursday by Médecins du Monde reported that 93 percent of pregnant or breastfeeding women had symptoms of anaemia, which is closely linked to malnutrition.  
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7de909a6-c463-11f1-88da-e362370cce2e/w:1024/p:16x9/d235e73d95d057b4dc09b314a270074be00fbad3.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7de909a6-c463-11f1-88da-e362370cce2e/w:1024/p:16x9/d235e73d95d057b4dc09b314a270074be00fbad3.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">7e873018-c463-11f1-9cfd-352276a81b64</guid><pubDate>Sat, 10 Oct 2026 04:31:42 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7de909a6-c463-11f1-88da-e362370cce2e/w:1024/p:16x9/d235e73d95d057b4dc09b314a270074be00fbad3.jpg">© Bashar Taleb, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>The World This Week</category><title>France protests, Israel's 'politically charged' remembrance, Ethiopia, Ukraine</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-world-this-week/20261009-france-protests-israel-s-politically-charged-remembrance-ethopia-ukraine</link><description>
It’s been a week of vigils, protests and political upheaval – from Israel, where three years after the Hamas-led attacks, former hostages and mourners called for accountability over the failures of October 7, as questions grow over the stalled path to peace in Gaza; to France, where mass demonstrations over chronic underfunding and poor conditions have drawn students, unions and hundreds of thousands of protesters into the streets, just months ahead of a presidential election. In Spain, Prime Minister Pedro Sánchez has made the housing crisis the centrepiece of a high-stakes electoral gamble, as protests intensify following the death of a pensioner whose eviction helped ignite the movement. And in the UK, questions remain over a suspected Iranian plot targeting US aircraft at RAF Fairford, after American B-1 bombers were hastily withdrawn amid warnings of a serious and immediate threat.
 

</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/84c2482c-c414-11f1-a7cb-29a2e29ae696/w:1024/p:16x9/DLS-PHOTO-MANIFS-FRANCE.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/84c2482c-c414-11f1-a7cb-29a2e29ae696/w:1024/p:16x9/DLS-PHOTO-MANIFS-FRANCE.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">40606eac-c40f-11f1-b42a-45f68a7aac1b</guid><pubDate>Fri, 09 Oct 2026 18:28:40 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Gavin LEE</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>FlyDubai co-pilot planned suicide attack on Tel Aviv airport inspired by 9/11, prosecutor says</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261009-flydubai-co-pilot-planned-suicide-attack-on-tel-aviv-airport-inspired-by-9-11</link><description>
The Omani co-pilot who attacked the captain of FlyDubai flight 1073 had planned to crash the plane into Tel Aviv's international airport in a suicide attack, the United Arab Emirates' top prosecutor said Friday. The Israel-bound flight carrying 182 people made an emergency landing in Saudi Arabia after a descent so extreme that part of its rudder was torn away. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/277fa400-c402-11f1-a1d2-e362370cce2e/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26273581638886-1.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/277fa400-c402-11f1-a1d2-e362370cce2e/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26273581638886-1.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">752941ba-c403-11f1-8cd8-9386513c9b90</guid><pubDate>Fri, 09 Oct 2026 17:04:15 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/277fa400-c402-11f1-a1d2-e362370cce2e/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26273581638886-1.jpg">© Ariel Schalit, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Tête à tête</category><title>Palestinians gained 'nothing' from October 7, Egyptian businessman Naguib Sawiris says</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/t%C3%AAte-%C3%A0-t%C3%AAte/20261008-palestinians-gained-nothing-from-october-7-egyptian-businessman-naguib-sawiris-says</link><description>
In an interview with FRANCE 24, Egyptian businessman Naguib Sawiris called the October 7 attacks a "horrible act of terrorism" that brought Palestinians "only destruction", while warning of an "expansionist" Israeli government. He also said that the economic fallout from the Iran war is already "happening", defended doubling his UAE investment despite the regional conflict, and praised Syria's new president.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7e5a9816-c254-11f1-8186-ff8cff4603f0/w:1024/p:16x9/FR-NW-PKG-EN-TETE-A-TETE-SAWIRIS-MIX-OK.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7e5a9816-c254-11f1-8186-ff8cff4603f0/w:1024/p:16x9/FR-NW-PKG-EN-TETE-A-TETE-SAWIRIS-MIX-OK.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">1da8cd78-c257-11f1-86e8-c5214af9e234</guid><pubDate>Thu, 08 Oct 2026 11:12:58 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Marc PERELMAN</dc:creator></item><item><category>Focus</category><title>Strait of Hormuz crisis fuels Cairo's plastic recycling business</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261008-strait-of-hormuz-crisis-fuels-cairo-s-plastic-recycling-business</link><description>
In the heart of the Egyptian capital Cairo, within the labyrinthine streets of the Manshiyet Nasser district, nearly 120,000 residents process a third of the megacity's waste every day. Long marginalised, these informal recycling specialists are now undergoing a dramatic transformation due to geopolitical tensions in the Strait of Hormuz, through which polyethylene from the Gulf usually passes.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4f3e140a-c2f8-11f1-9d0f-27c2853ad5a5/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-21204913886ac75e5b296d82-03546754.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4f3e140a-c2f8-11f1-9d0f-27c2853ad5a5/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-21204913886ac75e5b296d82-03546754.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4befadc0-c26e-11f1-afdc-05f01c7b4ba4</guid><pubDate>Thu, 08 Oct 2026 09:44:31 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Mathilde DELVIGNE</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Diplomats take shelter in Saudi capital as Yemen's Houthis target Riyadh airport</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261008-diplomats-school-pupils-take-shelter-in-saudi-capital-as-yemen-s-houthis-step-up-attacks</link><description>
Foreign diplomats and international schools in the Saudi capital took safety measures on Thursday as loud blasts rattled the city and Yemen's Houthi rebels claimed missile attacks against its airport. In a further blow to Riyadh, Turkey ruled out sending troops to confront the Iran-backed militia, despite a defence pact with Saudi Arabia.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/569c98ee-c31a-11f1-9635-c55799ef8309/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26276415281654-1.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/569c98ee-c31a-11f1-9635-c55799ef8309/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26276415281654-1.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">8ba344a0-c2f9-11f1-91b8-dfc25fb90ac8</guid><pubDate>Thu, 08 Oct 2026 09:20:46 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/569c98ee-c31a-11f1-9635-c55799ef8309/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26276415281654-1.jpg">© Stringer, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>'Most Israeli citizens lost confidence' in govt: Leaders 'shift' blame, 'block' commission inquiry</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/most-israeli-citizens-lost-confidence-in-govt-pm-leaders-shift-blame-block-commission-inquiry</link><description>
Oliver Farry welcomes Guy Poran, a former Israeli Air Force officer and member of Mistaclim (Looking the Occupation in the Eye). Poran sees October 7 as a profound rupture in Israeli society following the unprecedented Hamas attack, which targeted civilians across generations. He argues that responsibility for the failures cannot be separated from the policies that preceded the attack, including the Netanyahu government's approach toward Hamas. Without political change, Poran sees little prospect of repairing relations between Israelis and Palestinians or creating the conditions for a lasting peace, which he regards as crucial to Israel's future.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a5aaf096-c2db-11f1-87fc-27c2853ad5a5/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261007-080628-081900-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a5aaf096-c2db-11f1-87fc-27c2853ad5a5/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261007-080628-081900-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">abddb3ae-c2db-11f1-8bb6-d1909eeee128</guid><pubDate>Thu, 08 Oct 2026 07:42:49 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Explosions heard in Saudi capital Riyadh after Houthis' deadly attacks on airports</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261008-saudi-arabia-strikes-deadly-houthi-attacks-airports</link><description>
Several explosions were reported on Thursday in Saudi Arabia’s capital Riyadh amid ongoing fighting between the kingdom and Yemen's Houthis. A day earlier, three people were killed and 36 wounded in attacks on Abha and Riyadh’s King Khalid international airports claimed by the Iran-backed rebel group.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/40a51f4e-b423-11f1-bcd8-ed3d9e22a40f/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-19T114802Z-1980126111-RC28MNAXZ2HR-RTRMADP-3-IRAN-CRISIS-SAUDI-YEMEN.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/40a51f4e-b423-11f1-bcd8-ed3d9e22a40f/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-19T114802Z-1980126111-RC28MNAXZ2HR-RTRMADP-3-IRAN-CRISIS-SAUDI-YEMEN.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">6e3a1a14-c2a5-11f1-8b84-f3df44e11860</guid><pubDate>Thu, 08 Oct 2026 03:02:35 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/40a51f4e-b423-11f1-bcd8-ed3d9e22a40f/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-19T114802Z-1980126111-RC28MNAXZ2HR-RTRMADP-3-IRAN-CRISIS-SAUDI-YEMEN.jpg">© Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>The Debate</category><title>No longer the same Israel? October 7 and the future of the Jewish State</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20261007-no-longer-the-same-israel-october-7th-and-the-future-of-the-jewish-state</link><description>
For now, it's still Benjamin Netanyahu's Israel. In 2023, in the immediate aftermath of the country's worst day of bloodshed in its history, pundits predicted the quick demise of the right-wing prime minister. But on the third anniversary of the October 7 attacks, Israel's still not reckoned with the security failures on the day, the root causes of the Hamas-led terror attack, the brutal war of vengeance that followed and above all, Netanyahu is still prime minister with a fair shot at re-election. Even if the Likud leader is voted out on October 27, his most serious election rivals don't exactly advocate for a radical break when it comes to the Palestinians.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f146ff42-c275-11f1-932d-4b195755b8ed/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-07T051408Z-2040734097-RC23YNA0KTNJ-RTRMADP-3-ISRAEL-PALESTINIANS-NOVA.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f146ff42-c275-11f1-932d-4b195755b8ed/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-07T051408Z-2040734097-RC23YNA0KTNJ-RTRMADP-3-ISRAEL-PALESTINIANS-NOVA.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">5aee654e-c275-11f1-82a1-d551fdd35c45</guid><pubDate>Wed, 07 Oct 2026 22:10:13 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>François PICARD</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Israel marks three years since October 7 attacks with strikes on Gaza, political debate</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261007-israel-three-years-october-7-attack-elections</link><description>
Israel marked the third anniversary of Hamas’s October 7 attack on Wednesday with gatherings in tribute and renewed strikes on Gaza as political debate intensified ahead of elections. Gaza officials said strikes on the territory had killed five people despite a year-old ceasefire agreement.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9ff484f6-c271-11f1-b4b1-27c2853ad5a5/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D2H22CT.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9ff484f6-c271-11f1-b4b1-27c2853ad5a5/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D2H22CT.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a8026040-c295-11f1-9109-dd7e32cd65fc</guid><pubDate>Wed, 07 Oct 2026 21:50:07 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9ff484f6-c271-11f1-b4b1-27c2853ad5a5/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D2H22CT.jpg">© AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>'It's still unclear whether Netanyahu will pay for what happened during his time in office'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/it-s-still-unclear-whether-netanyahu-will-pay-for-what-happened-during-his-time-in-office</link><description>
As Israel marks the third anniversary of the October 7 attacks, questions linger about the warnings Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu received about them. Speaking with FRANCE 24's Mark Owen, Ayala Panievsky, Lecturer at City University of London and author of The New Censorship, explains that the allegations in the run-up to the elections "are very damaging for Netanyahu but there are some factors mitigating the risk for him", including a fragmented opposition as well as the control of major media.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/be013ffa-bc7e-11f1-adb1-177f79e345bf/w:1024/p:16x9/AP25357403714237.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/be013ffa-bc7e-11f1-adb1-177f79e345bf/w:1024/p:16x9/AP25357403714237.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">1be11542-c287-11f1-8caf-a909ffd0bc14</guid><pubDate>Wed, 07 Oct 2026 19:52:06 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>'Resilience' of Israelis as they mourn the loss of loved ones and 'the sense that we can be safe'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261007-resilience-of-israelis-as-they-the-mourn-loss-of-loved-ones-and-the-sense-that-we-can-be-safe</link><description>
Angela Diffley is pleased to welcome Dr. Danny Brom, Founding Director of METIV, the Israel Psychotrauma Center in Jerusalem. According to Dr. Brom, as Israelis and Jewish people around the world continue to mourn the largest loss of Jewish life on a single day since the Holocaust, their fundamental sense of collective security has also been shattered. What strikes him, however, is the resilience that exists alongside the grieving. How can individuals, communities and society rebuild a sense of safety without allowing fear to dictate the future? Yet, as Dr. Brom observes, “the war is still going on,” while political leaders speak of pursuing “the ultimate victory, which no one really knows what that is.”
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4e9b41c6-c271-11f1-8565-4b195755b8ed/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261007-150336-152020-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4e9b41c6-c271-11f1-8565-4b195755b8ed/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261007-150336-152020-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">54563e86-c271-11f1-909c-55ad73d50d7a</guid><pubDate>Wed, 07 Oct 2026 17:46:29 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>October 7: Former Israeli hostage speaks to France 24</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261007-october-7-former-israeli-hostage-speaks-to-france-24</link><description>
“The terrorists pulled us out through the window. They handcuffed me and pushed us into a car that they had brought from Gaza.”
 
Former Israeli hostage Shoshan Haran speaks to France 24.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/158ad354-c255-11f1-9037-0f96b136895a/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-ISRAELI-HOSTAGE-tiktok-00-00-12-07-Still004.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/158ad354-c255-11f1-9037-0f96b136895a/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-ISRAELI-HOSTAGE-tiktok-00-00-12-07-Still004.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">3ea01bca-c253-11f1-9c88-e5b444f805de</guid><pubDate>Wed, 07 Oct 2026 13:30:20 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Perspective</category><title>'Time doesn't heal': Parents of October 7 attacks victim Aner Shapira</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/perspective/20261007-time-doesn-t-heal-parents-of-aner-shapira-killed-on-october-7-2023</link><description>
The parents of a 22-year-old Israeli man who was killed when Hamas attacked the Nova music festival on October 7, 2023 have told FRANCE 24 how they can still feel him surrounding them even though he's no longer here. Shira and Moshe Shapira say that time doesn't heal, but they are learning how to live with their loss. Their son Aner managed to throw seven grenades back towards Hamas fighters, before an eighth exploded in his hands, killing him. They spoke to us in Perspective.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/357ef1f8-c24c-11f1-ac38-0f96b136895a/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-14306598286ac63d9f40c3f4-70504155.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/357ef1f8-c24c-11f1-ac38-0f96b136895a/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-14306598286ac63d9f40c3f4-70504155.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f877ebd4-c23c-11f1-ade5-cdcea157df53</guid><pubDate>Wed, 07 Oct 2026 12:59:46 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Stuart NORVAL</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>October 7: Israelis mark three years since Hamas attacks</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261007-october-7-israelis-mark-three-years-since-hamas-attacks</link><description>
Israel is marking the third anniversary of the October 7, 2023, Hamas terrorist attack on Wednesday with memorials across the country.
 
At the site of the Nova music festival, where more than 300 people were killed, families gathered at dawn for a moment of silence and paid tribute in front of portraits both of festival-goers and security forces who died on October 7.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bdca8f88-c236-11f1-852d-b942c38e4bd7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26280153593942.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bdca8f88-c236-11f1-852d-b942c38e4bd7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26280153593942.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e43228ae-c23e-11f1-9258-a39aff491d10</guid><pubDate>Wed, 07 Oct 2026 11:04:39 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item></channel></rss>
